    "assessment": "The swing level computation uses a centered window that extends 5 bars forward from the reference point. When computing swing_high[i-1], the window includes bars up to i-1+5 = i+4. This means bar i's HIGH is included in the swing level. However, the signal condition compares close[i] (current close) against swing_high[i-1] (previous bar's confirmed level). The critical question is whether knowing bar i's high at the time of the close creates a lookahead bias. In standard OHLC data, the high is known at bar close, so this is NOT a lookahead violation. The signal is available at bar close.",
